## 📏 The Scoring Model

Every risk is scored on **Likelihood (1–5)** and **Impact (1–5)**. The score is `Likelihood × Impact` (1–25), bucketed into a rating. The anchors below are what make scoring *repeatable* — without them, two reviewers score the same risk differently.

### Likelihood anchors

| Score | Label | Anchor |
|-------|-------|--------|
| 1 | Rare | No known occurrence; would require multiple controls to fail |
| 2 | Unlikely | Possible but not expected in normal operation |
| 3 | Possible | Could occur within a 12-month window |
| 4 | Likely | Expected to occur without additional controls |
| 5 | Almost certain | Already occurring or occurs frequently |

### Impact anchors

| Score | Label | Anchor (harm to individuals, org, or rights) |
|-------|-------|--------|
| 1 | Negligible | Minor inconvenience, no rights impact, trivial cost |
| 2 | Minor | Limited harm to a few users, easily reversible |
| 3 | Moderate | Material harm to a group, reputational hit, some regulatory interest |
| 4 | Major | Serious harm to individuals' rights, regulatory action, significant loss |
| 5 | Severe | Widespread harm, safety impact, fundamental-rights violation, existential legal exposure |

### Rating bands

| Score (L×I) | Rating | Required Action | SLA to treat |
|-------------|--------|-----------------|--------------|
| 1–4 | 🟢 Low | Accept & monitor | Next review cycle |
| 5–9 | 🟡 Moderate | Treat with standard controls | 90 days |
| 10–15 | 🟠 High | Treat; requires governance-board visibility | 30 days |
| 16–25 | 🔴 Critical | Do not deploy / halt until mitigated | Immediate |

