## 🗂️ The Register Schema (Columns)

Copy these columns into a spreadsheet or GRC tool. Each row is one risk on one AI system.

| Field | Description |
|-------|-------------|
| **Risk ID** | Unique key, e.g. `AIR-2026-001` |
| **AI System / Use Case** | The system this risk attaches to |
| **Lifecycle Stage** | Design / Data / Train / Validate / Deploy / Monitor / Retire |
| **Risk Category** | One of the 8 taxonomy categories |
| **Risk Description** | Plain-language "what could go wrong and why" |
| **Cause / Trigger** | The condition that would realize the risk |
| **Potential Impact** | Who is harmed and how |
| **Inherent Likelihood** | 1–5 (before controls) |
| **Inherent Impact** | 1–5 (before controls) |
| **Inherent Score** | L × I |
| **Existing Controls** | Controls already in place |
| **Residual Likelihood / Impact / Score** | 1–5 each, after controls |
| **Risk Owner** | Named accountable person (not a team) |
| **Treatment Decision** | Accept / Mitigate / Transfer / Avoid |
| **Treatment Actions** | Specific tasks + due dates |
| **Framework Mapping** | ISO 42001 clause / NIST AI RMF function / EU AI Act article |
| **Status** | Open / In Treatment / Monitoring / Closed |
| **Last Reviewed / Next Review** | Dates |

