## 🧪 Worked Examples

### AIR-2026-001 — RAG customer-support chatbot

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Risk Category | Security (prompt injection) |
| Description | Malicious user embeds instructions in a support ticket that the bot ingests via retrieval, causing it to reveal internal system prompt / other customers' data |
| Inherent L×I | 4 × 4 = **16 🔴 Critical** |
| Existing Controls | Input sanitization, retrieval scoping to tenant |
| Residual L×I | 2 × 4 = **8 🟡 Moderate** |
| Owner | Head of Support Platform |
| Treatment | Mitigate — add output filtering, prompt-injection eval in CI, human escalation path |
| Mapping | NIST AI RMF *Manage 2.3*; OWASP LLM01; EU AI Act Art. 15 (accuracy & robustness) |

### AIR-2026-002 — HR résumé-screening model

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Risk Category | Bias & Fairness |
| Description | Model trained on historical hiring data reproduces past demographic skew, down-ranking qualified candidates from underrepresented groups |
| Inherent L×I | 4 × 5 = **20 🔴 Critical** |
| Existing Controls | None at intake |
| Residual L×I | 2 × 4 = **8 🟡 Moderate** |
| Owner | VP People + AI Governance Lead (joint) |
| Treatment | Mitigate — fairness testing across protected groups, human-in-the-loop for all rejects, quarterly disparate-impact audit |
| Mapping | ISO 42001 A.6.2 (impact assessment); EU AI Act Annex III (high-risk: employment); NIST AI RMF *Measure 2.11* |

### AIR-2026-003 — Third-party GenAI connector (SaaS)

| Field | Value |
|-------|-------|
| Risk Category | Third-Party & Supply Chain |
| Description | Enterprise data routed to an external GenAI vendor whose data-use, retention, and sub-processor terms are opaque; vendor may train on inputs |
| Inherent L×I | 3 × 4 = **12 🟠 High** |
| Existing Controls | DPA in place |
| Residual L×I | 2 × 3 = **6 🟡 Moderate** |
| Owner | Procurement + CISO delegate |
| Treatment | Mitigate — contractual no-train clause, data-minimization at the boundary, vendor SOC 2 + AI addendum review, kill-switch |
| Mapping | ISO 42001 A.10 (third-party); ISO 27001 A.5.19; EU AI Act Art. 25 (obligations along value chain) |

